Id: cron003f
Severity: FAIL
Category: cron
Check: check_crontabs
Fix: chmod go-w the program, and the directories on the way to it.
References: crontab(5)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST AC-3, CM-5, CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

The listed cron entry uses a file or executable which has group write
permissions, world write permissions or both.  This can allow the
system to be compromised.  For root cron entries, this is especially
dangerous.  Note that the actual problem may be with a directory in
the path to the file, not the file itself.

It is a FAIL because anyone on the system can write it and the file
named is executable.

Until 3.4.0 this was reported as cron003, without the letter for its level.
